			"widgets_values":[
				"How the reference pictures align with the target video — Picture 1 (from Shot 1) aligns with the 0.00-second mark of the target video; Picture 2 (from Shot 1) aligns with the 8.00-second mark of the target video.\n\nintegrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Live-action cinematic paper-craft horror in a continuous first-person POV begins in the exact close framing established by Picture 1. The woman's right fingertips press into the torn eye opening, bending the layered paper rim inward as loose fibers stretch and the bamboo armature flexes. The camera pushes forward with large amplitude at accelerating speed, following the hand directly through the eye opening. The circular rim expands around the frame and sweeps past the lens, revealing a narrow tunnel formed by overlapping paper layers and curved bamboo strips. A single red lantern remains centered on the vanishing point and grows rapidly while cold light falls away and red reflected light travels across the paper fibers. The camera passes the lantern and bursts through the far end of the tunnel into open space above the paper funeral city. The torn exit rim streams past the outer edges of the frame, the woman's hand reaches forward, and the camera settles into the wide elevated POV, depth, lighting, and final composition established by Picture 2.\n\noverall_soundscape: Dry paper fibers crackle close to the microphone as the hand presses forward, followed by the creak of bending bamboo and a rising rush of air through the narrow tunnel. The exit opens into distant wind, hundreds of softly rattling paper lanterns, and a deep wooden impact from somewhere in the city below.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: A sustained low bowed-metal drone begins quietly, joined by a rapidly accelerating pulse during the tunnel passage and one resonant bass strike as the paper city is revealed.",
